{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P43jFayNqsrGkVoxah2Eof","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# shift_reg\n2\t\n3\tAn 8-bit bidirectional shift register with synchronous parallel load, serial input and serial output.\n4\t\n5\t## Ports\n6\t| Port  | Dir | Width | Description |\n7\t|-------|-----|-------|-------------|\n8\t| clk   | in  | 1     | Rising-edge clock |\n9\t| rst_n | in  | 1     | Asynchronous active-low reset |\n10\t| en    | in  | 1     | Shift enable |\n11\t| load  | in  | 1     | Synchronous parallel load |\n12\t| dir   | in  | 1     | Shift direction: 0 = left (toward bit 7), 1 = right (toward bit 0) |\n13\t| sin   | in  | 1     | Serial input |\n14\t| d     | in  | 8     | Parallel load data |\n15\t| q     | out | 8     | Register contents (registered) |\n16\t| sout  | out | 1     | Serial output (combinational) |\n17\t\n18\t## Behavior\n19\t- While `rst_n` is low, `q` is 0.\n20\t- On a rising edge of `clk`, in priority order:\n21\t  1. If `load` is high, `q <= d`. **`load` does not depend on `en`**: a load happens whenever\n22\t     `load` is high, whether `en` is high or low.\n23\t  2. Else if `en` is high and `dir` is 0 (shift left): `q <= {q[6:0], sin}`.\n24\t  3. Else if `en` is high and `dir` is 1 (shift right): `q <= {sin, q[7:1]}`.\n25\t  4. Otherwise `q` holds.\n26\t- `sout` is the bit that will be shifted out by the next shift in the currently selected\n27\t  direction: `sout = q[7]` when `dir` is 0, and `sout = q[0]` when `dir` is 1. It depends only\n28\t  on `q` and `dir` (not on `en` or `load`).\n29\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1fe6d0c8-56b1-4147-8b28-1192a39b8b69","uuid":"2f8c15e2-811e-4198-a643-bbcfc51899ff","timestamp":"2026-10-19T23:42:05.923Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\abhig\\Documents\\New folder\\assay\\runs\\v2__shift_reg__t2\\workspace\\spec.md","content":"# shift_reg\n\nAn 8-bit bidirectional shift register with synchronous parallel load, serial input and serial output.\n\n## Ports\n| Port  | Dir | Width | Description |\n|-------|-----|-------|-------------|\n| clk   | in  | 1     | Rising-edge clock |\n| rst_n | in  | 1     | Asynchronous active-low reset |\n| en    | in  | 1     | Shift enable |\n| load  | in  | 1     | Synchronous parallel load |\n| dir   | in  | 1     | Shift direction: 0 = left (toward bit 7), 1 = right (toward bit 0) |\n| sin   | in  | 1     | Serial input |\n| d     | in  | 8     | Parallel load data |\n| q     | out | 8     | Register contents (registered) |\n| sout  | out | 1     | Serial output (combinational) |\n\n## Behavior\n- While `rst_n` is low, `q` is 0.\n- On a rising edge of `clk`, in priority order:\n  1. If `load` is high, `q <= d`. **`load` does not depend on `en`**: a load happens whenever\n     `load` is high, whether `en` is high or low.\n  2. Else if `en` is high and `dir` is 0 (shift left): `q <= {q[6:0], sin}`.\n  3. Else if `en` is high and `dir` is 1 (shift right): `q <= {sin, q[7:1]}`.\n  4. Otherwise `q` holds.\n- `sout` is the bit that will be shifted out by the next shift in the currently selected\n  direction: `sout = q[7]` when `dir` is 0, and `sout = q[0]` when `dir` is 1. It depends only\n  on `q` and `dir` (not on `en` or `load`).\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}}}
